\subsection{Dispersion Relation Derivation}

In flat spacetime ($R = 0$), expand around vacuum $\Psi = v + \phi$:

\begin{equation}
\square\phi + \left[m_{\text{eff}}^2 + 2\lambda v^2\right]\phi + \text{(higher orders)} = 0
\end{equation}

Plane wave ansatz $\phi \sim e^{i(k\cdot x - \omega t)}$ yields:

\begin{equation}
\omega^2 = k^2 + m_{\text{eff}}^2 + 2\lambda v^2
\end{equation}

In curved spacetime with non-minimal coupling:

\begin{equation}
\omega_n^2 = k_n^2 + m_{\text{eff}}^2 + 2\xi R + 2\lambda v^2
\end{equation}

For cavity modes with boundary conditions, $k_n = n\pi/L$:

\begin{equation}
\omega_n = \sqrt{\frac{n^2\pi^2}{L^2} + m_{\text{eff}}^2 + 2\xi R + 2\lambda v^2}
\end{equation}

